.TH LALINFERENCE_BENCH "1" "January 2026" "LALInference" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalinference_bench \- a program from LALInference
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Data Parameters \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.IP
Options for reading/generating data. User should specify which interferometers
to use and their data source using the following options. The data source
can be either a LFS cache file (generated by gw_data_find) with channel name
(e.g. \fB\-\-H1\-cache\fR H1.cache \fB\-\-H1\-channel\fR H1:DCS\-CALIB\-STRAIN_C02 )
or internally\-generated gaussian noise with a given detector PSD model
(e.g. \fB\-\-H1\-cache\fR LALSimAdLIGO \fB\-\-dataseed\fR 1234)
or by searching for frame files in the local directory
(e.g. \fB\-\-glob\-frame\-data\fR \fB\-\-H1\-channel\fR H1:DCS\-CALIB\-STRAIN_C02)
.IP
Additional noise curves for simulated data can be specified by providing
their PSD or ASD as a text file. See detailed options below.
.HP
\fB\-\-ifo\fR IFO1 [\-\-ifo IFO2 ...] IFOs can be H1,L1,V1
.TP
\fB\-\-IFO1\-cache\fR cache1
Cache files
.TP
[\-\-IFO2\-cache2 cache2 ...]
lal PSDs: LAL{Ad}LIGO, LALVirgo
lalsimuation PSDs: LALSim{Ad}LIGO, LALSim{Ad}Virgo
interpolate from file: interp:asd_file.txt
.TP
\fB\-\-psdstart\fR GPStime
GPS start time of PSD estimation data
.TP
\fB\-\-psdlength\fR length
Length of PSD estimation data in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-seglen\fR length
Length of segments for PSD estimation and analysis in seconds
.TP
(\fB\-\-glob\-frame\-data\fR)
Will search for frame files containing data in the PWD.
Filenames must begin with the IFO's 1\-letter code, e.g. H\-*.gwf
.TP
(\fB\-\-dont\-dump\-extras\fR)
If given, won't save PSD and SNR files
.TP
(\fB\-\-dump\-geocenter\-pols\fR)
If given, print out the TD/FD h_plus and h_cross polarisations
.TP
(\fB\-\-trigtime\fR GPStime)
GPS time of the trigger to analyse
.IP
(optional when using \fB\-\-margtime\fR or \fB\-\-margtimephi\fR)
.TP
(\fB\-\-segment\-start\fR)
GPS time of the start of the segment
.TP
(optional with \fB\-\-trigtime\fR,
default: seglen\-2 s before \fB\-\-trigtime\fR)
.TP
(\fB\-\-srate\fR rate)
Downsample data to rate in Hz (4096.0,)
.TP
(\fB\-\-padding\fR PAD [sec]
Override default 0.4 seconds padding
.TP
(\fB\-\-injectionsrate\fR rate)
Downsample injection signal to rate in Hz (\fB\-\-srate\fR)
.TP
(\fB\-\-IFO1\-flow\fR freq1
Specify lower frequency cutoff for overlap integral (20.0)
.IP
[\-\-IFO2\-flow freq2 ...])
.TP
(\fB\-\-IFO1\-fhigh\fR freq1
Specify higher frequency cutoff for overlap integral (Nyquist
.TP
[\-\-IFO2\-fhigh freq2 ...])
freq 0.5*srate)
.TP
(\fB\-\-IFO1\-channel\fR chan1
Specify channel names when reading cache files
.IP
[\-\-IFO2\-channel chan2 ...])
.TP
(\fB\-\-IFO1\-asd\fR asd1\-ascii.txt
Read in ASD from ascii file. This is not equivalent
.TP
[\-\-IFO2\-asd asd2\-ascii.txt ...])
to using \fB\-\-IFO1\-cache\fR interp:asd_file.txt since the former
won't use the ascii ASD to generate fake noise.
.TP
(\fB\-\-IFO1\-psd\fR psd1\-ascii.txt
Read in PSD from ascii file. This is not equivalent
.TP
[\-\-IFO2\-psd psd2\-ascii.txt ...])
to using \fB\-\-IFO1\-cache\fR interp:asd_file.txt since the former
won't use the ascii PSD to generate fake noise.
.TP
(\fB\-\-dataseed\fR number)
Specify random seed to use when generating data
.TP
(\fB\-\-lalinspiralinjection\fR)
Enables injections via the LALInspiral package
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-fref\fR)
Reference frequency of parameters in injection XML (default 100Hz)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-lambda1\fR)
value of lambda1 to be injected, LALSimulation only (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-lambda2\fR)
value of lambda2 to be injected, LALSimulation only (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-lambdaT\fR
value of lambdaT to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-dlambdaT\fR
value of dlambdaT to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-logp1\fR)
value of logp1 to be injected
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-gamma1\fR)
value of gamma1 to be injected
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-gamma2\fR)
value of gamma2 to be injected
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-gamma3\fR)
value of gamma3 to be injected
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-SDgamma0\fR)
value of SDgamma0 to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-SDgamma1\fR)
value of SDgamma1 to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-SDgamma2\fR)
value of SDgamma2 to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-SDgamma3\fR)
value of SDgamma3 to be injected (0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-spinOrder\fR PNorder)
Specify twice the injection PN order (e.g. 5 <==> 2.5PN)
.TP
of spin effects effects to use, only for LALSimulation
(default: \fB\-1\fR <==> Use all spin effects).
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-tidalOrder\fR PNorder)
Specify twice the injection PN order (e.g. 10 <==> 5PN)
.TP
of tidal effects to use, only for LALSimulation
(default: \fB\-1\fR <==> Use all tidal effects).
.TP
(\fB\-\-inj\-spin\-frame\fR FRAME
Specify injection spin frame: choice of total\-j, orbital\-l, view.
.IP
(Default = OrbitalL).
.IP
(\fB\-\-inj\-numreldata\fR FileName) Location of NR data file for the injection of NR waveforms (with NR_hdf5 in injection XML file).
(\fB\-\-0noise\fR)                  Sets the noise realisation to be identically zero
.IP
(for the fake caches above only)
.PP
lalinference_bench: Benchmark template and likelihood functions.
.IP
Options:
.TP
\fB\-\-Niter\fR
: Number of calls to time (delfault 1000)
.TP
\fB\-\-bench\-template\fR
: Only benchmark template function
.TP
\fB\-\-bench\-likelihood\fR : Only benchmark likelihood function
(defaults to benchmarking both)
.IP
Example (for 1.0\-1.0 binary with seglen 8, srate 4096):
$ ./lalinference_bench \fB\-\-psdlength\fR 1000 \fB\-\-psdstart\fR 1 \fB\-\-seglen\fR 8 \fB\-\-srate\fR 4096 \fB\-\-trigtime\fR 0 \fB\-\-ifo\fR H1 \fB\-\-H1\-channel\fR LALSimAdLIGO \fB\-\-H1\-cache\fR LALSimAdLIGO \fB\-\-dataseed\fR 1324 \fB\-\-Niter\fR 10000 \fB\-\-fix\-chirpmass\fR 1.218 \fB\-\-fix\-q\fR 1.0
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Injection Arguments \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.IP
(\fB\-\-inj\fR injections.xml) Injection XML file to use
(\fB\-\-event\fR N)            Event number from Injection XML file to use
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Template Arguments \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.TP
(\fB\-\-use\-eta\fR)
Jump in symmetric mass ratio eta, instead of q=m1/m2 (m1>m2)
.TP
(\fB\-\-approx\fR)
Specify a template approximant and phase order to use
.TP
(default TaylorF2threePointFivePN). Available approximants:
default modeldomain="time": GeneratePPN, TaylorT1, TaylorT2,
.TP
TaylorT3, TaylorT4, EOB, EOBNR,
EOBNRv2, EOBNRv2HM, SEOBNRv1,
SpinTaylor, SpinQuadTaylor,
SpinTaylorFrameless, SpinTaylorT4,
PhenSpinTaylorRD, NumRel.
.TP
default modeldomain="frequency": TaylorF1, TaylorF2, TaylorF2RedSpin,
TaylorF2RedSpinTidal, IMRPhenomA,
IMRPhenomB, IMRPhenomP, IMRPhenomPv2.
.TP
(\fB\-\-amporder\fR PNorder)
Specify a PN order in amplitude to use (defaults: LALSimulation: max available; LALInspiral: newtownian).
.TP
(\fB\-\-fref\fR f_ref)
Specify a reference frequency at which parameters are defined (default 100).
.TP
(\fB\-\-tidal\fR)
Enables tidal corrections, only with LALSimulation.
.TP
(\fB\-\-tidalT\fR)
Enables reparmeterized tidal corrections, only with LALSimulation.
.TP
(\fB\-\-4PolyEOS\fR)
Enables 4\-piece polytropic EOS parmeterization, only with LALSimulation.
.TP
(\fB\-\-4SpectralDecomp\fR)
Enables 4\-coeff. spectral decomposition EOS parmeterization, only with LALSimulation.
.TP
(\fB\-\-eos\fR
EOS)               Fix the neutron star EOS. Use "\-\-eos help" for allowed names
.TP
(\fB\-\-BinaryLove\fR)
Enable the Binary Neutron Star common EoS tidal model, expressed through EOS\-insensitive relations
.TP
(\fB\-\-spinOrder\fR PNorder)
Specify twice the PN order (e.g. 5 <==> 2.5PN) of spin effects to use, only for LALSimulation (default: \fB\-1\fR <==> Use all spin effects).
.TP
(\fB\-\-tidalOrder\fR PNorder)
Specify twice the PN order (e.g. 10 <==> 5PN) of tidal effects to use, only for LALSimulation (default: \fB\-1\fR <==> Use all tidal effects).
.TP
(\fB\-\-numreldata\fR FileName)
Location of NR data file for NR waveforms (with NR_hdf5 approx).
.TP
(\fB\-\-modeldomain\fR)
domain the waveform template will be computed in ("time" or "frequency"). If not given will use LALSim to decide
.TP
(\fB\-\-spinAligned\fR or \fB\-\-aligned\-spin\fR)
template will assume spins aligned with the orbital angular momentum.
.TP
(\fB\-\-singleSpin\fR)
template will assume only the spin of the most massive binary component exists.
.TP
(\fB\-\-noSpin\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-spin\fR)
template will assume no spins (giving this will void spinOrder!=0)
.TP
(\fB\-\-no\-detector\-frame\fR)
model will NOT use detector\-centred coordinates and instead RA,dec
.IP
(\fB\-\-nonGR_alpha\fR value) this is a LIV parameter which should only be passed when log10lambda_eff/lambda_eff is passed as a grtest\-parameter for LIV test
(\fB\-\-LIV_A_sign\fR) this is a LIV parameter determining if +A or \fB\-A\fR is being tested; A occurs in the modified dispersion relation. LIV_A_sign has to be either +1 or \fB\-1\fR
(\fB\-\-liv\fR) this flag is now needed for launching a LIV run
(\fB\-\-grtest\-parameters\fR dchi0,..,dxi1,..,dalpha1,..) template will assume deformations in the corresponding phase coefficients.
(\fB\-\-generic\-fd\-correction\fR) enables the generic frequency domain corrections to the template phase.
(\fB\-\-generic\-fd\-correction\-hm\fR) apply generic frequency domain corrections to higher\-modes waveform.
(\fB\-\-generic\-fd\-correction\-window\fR) sets the fraction of the peak frequency up to which the generic phase corrections are applied (default=1).
(\fB\-\-generic\-fd\-correction\-ncycles\fR) sets the number of  cycles for the tapering of the generic phase corrections (default=1).
(\fB\-\-ppe\-parameters\fR aPPE1,....     template will assume the presence of an arbitrary number of PPE parameters. They must be paired correctly.
(\fB\-\-modeList\fR lm,l\-m...,lm,l\-m)           List of modes to be used by the model. The chosen modes ('lm') should be passed as a ',' seperated list.
(\fB\-\-phenomXHMMband\fR float)     Threshold parameter for the Multibanding of the non\-precessing hlm modes in IMRPhenomXHM and IMRPhenomXPHM. If set to 0 then do not use multibanding.
.IP
Options and default values can be found in https://lscsoft.docs.ligo.org/lalsuite/lalsimulation/group___l_a_l_sim_i_m_r_phenom_x__c.html
.TP
(\fB\-\-phenomXPHMMband\fR float)
Threshold parameter for the Multibanding of the Euler angles in IMRPhenomXPHM. If set to 0 then do not use multibanding.
Options and default values can be found in https://lscsoft.docs.ligo.org/lalsuite/lalsimulation/group___l_a_l_sim_i_m_r_phenom_x__c.html
.TP
(\fB\-\-phenomXPFinalSpinMod\fR int) Change version for the final spin model used in IMRPhenomXP/IMRPhenomXPHM.
Options and default values can be found in https://lscsoft.docs.ligo.org/lalsuite/lalsimulation/group___l_a_l_sim_i_m_r_phenom_x__c.html
.TP
(\fB\-\-phenomXPrecVersion\fR int)
Change version of the Euler angles for the twisting\-up of IMRPhenomXP/IMRPhenomXPHM.
Options and default values can be found in https://lscsoft.docs.ligo.org/lalsuite/lalsimulation/group___l_a_l_sim_i_m_r_phenom_x__c.html
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Starting Parameters \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.IP
You can generally have MCMC chains to start from a given parameter value by using \fB\-\-parname\fR VALUE. Names currently known to the code are:
.TP
time
Waveform time (overrides random about trigtime).
.TP
chirpmass
Chirpmass
.TP
eta
Symmetric massratio (needs \fB\-\-use\-eta\fR)
.TP
q
Asymmetric massratio (a.k.a. q=m2/m1 with m1>m2)
.TP
phase
Coalescence phase.
.TP
costheta_jn
Cosine of angle between J and line of sight [rads]
.TP
logdistance
Log Distance (requires \fB\-\-use\-logdistance\fR)
.TP
rightascension
Rightascensions
.TP
declination
Declination.
.TP
polarisation
Polarisation angle.
.IP
* Spin Parameters:
.TP
a_spin1
Spin1 magnitude
.TP
a_spin2
Spin2 magnitude
.TP
tilt_spin1
Angle between spin1 and orbital angular momentum
.TP
tilt_spin2
Angle between spin2 and orbital angular momentum
.TP
phi_12
Difference between spins' azimuthal angles
.TP
phi_jl
Difference between total and orbital angular momentum azimuthal angles
.IP
* Equation of State parameters:
.IP
(requires \fB\-\-tidal\fR)
lambda1                      lambda1.
lambda2                      lambda2.
(requires \fB\-\-tidalT\fR)
lambdaT                      lambdaT.
dLambdaT                     dLambdaT.
(requires \fB\-\-4PolyEOS\fR)
logp1                        logp1.
gamma1                       gamma1.
gamma2                       gamma2.
gamma3                       gamma3.
(requires \fB\-\-BinaryLove\fR)
lambdaS                      Symmetric tidal deformability.
(requires \fB\-\-4SpectralDecomp\fR):
SDgamma0                     SDgamma0.
SDgamma1                     SDgamma1.
SDgamma2                     SDgamma2.
SDgamma3                     SDgamma3.
.IP
*
* Spin\-induced quadrupole moment test parameters:
.IP
(requires \fB\-\-dQuadMon12\fR)
dQuadMon1                      dQuadMon1.
dQuadMon2                      dQuadMon2.
(requires \fB\-\-dQuadMonSA\fR)
dQuadMonS                      dQuadMonS.
dQuadMonA                      dQuadMonA.
.IP
(dQuadMonS and dQuadMonA are the symmetric and antisymmetric combinations of dQuadMon1 and dQuadMon2).
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
\fB\-\-\-\fR Prior Ranges \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
You can generally use \fB\-\-paramname\-min\fR MIN \fB\-\-paramname\-max\fR MAX to set the prior range for the parameter paramname
The names known to the code are listed below.
Component masses, total mass and time have dedicated options listed here:
.TP
(\fB\-\-trigtime\fR time)
Center of the prior for the time variable.
.TP
(\fB\-\-comp\-min\fR min)
Minimum component mass (1.0).
.TP
(\fB\-\-comp\-max\fR max)
Maximum component mass (100.0).
.TP
(\fB\-\-mass1\-min\fR min, \fB\-\-mass1\-max\fR max)
Min and max for mass1 (default: same as comp\-min,comp\-max, will over\-ride these.
.TP
(\fB\-\-mass2\-min\fR min, \fB\-\-mass2\-max\fR max)
Min and max for mass2 (default: same as comp\-min,comp\-max, will over\-ride these.
.TP
(\fB\-\-mtotal\-min\fR min)
Minimum total mass (2.0).
.TP
(\fB\-\-mtotal\-max\fR max)
Maximum total mass (200.0).
.TP
(\fB\-\-dt\fR time)
Width of time prior, centred around trigger (0.2s).
.TP
(\fB\-\-ns\-max\-mass\fR)
Maximum observed NS mass used for EOS prior (none).
.TP
(\fB\-\-varyFlow\fR, \fB\-\-flowMin\fR, \fB\-\-flowMax\fR)
Allow the lower frequency bound of integration to vary in given range.
.TP
(\fB\-\-pinparams\fR)
List of parameters to set to injected values [mchirp,asym_massratio,etc].
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Fix Parameters \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.IP
You can generally fix a parameter to be fixed to a given values by using \fB\-\-fix\-paramname\fR VALUE
where the known names have been listed above.
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\fR Likelihood Arguments \fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\fR
.TP
(\fB\-\-zeroLogLike\fR)
Use flat, null likelihood
.TP
(\fB\-\-studentTLikelihood\fR)
Use the Student\-T Likelihood that marginalizes over noise
.IP
(\fB\-\-correlatedGaussianLikelihood\fR) Use analytic, correlated Gaussian for Likelihood Z=\-21.3
(\fB\-\-bimodalGaussianLikelihood\fR)    Use analytic, bimodal correlated Gaussian for Likelihood Z=\-25.9
(\fB\-\-rosenbrockLikelihood\fR)         Use analytic, Rosenbrock banana for Likelihood
(\fB\-\-noiseonly\fR)                    Using noise\-only likelihood
(\fB\-\-margphi\fR)                      Using marginalised phase likelihood
(\fB\-\-margtime\fR)                     Using marginalised time likelihood
(\fB\-\-margtimephi\fR)                  Using marginalised in time and phase likelihood
(\fB\-\-margdist\fR)                     Using marginalisation in distance with d^2 prior (compatible with \fB\-\-margphi\fR and \fB\-\-margtimephi\fR)
(\fB\-\-margdist\-comoving\fR)            Using marginalisation in distance with uniform\-in\-comoving\-volume prior (compatible with \fB\-\-margphi\fR and \fB\-\-margtimephi\fR)
